UPDATE posts SET content = $tag4$<p><strong>Dikkat spoiler içerir!</strong></p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote has-text-align-center"><p>Duyulmak istiyorsan sesini yükseltmelisin.</p></blockquote>



<p>Senaryosunu Jack Thorne’un yazığı Nancy Springer’ın romanınından uyarlanan Enola Holmes filmi, Netflix ile izleyicisiyle buluştu. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/enola-holmes-538x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4043" width="302" height="576"/></figure>



<p>Nancy Springer'ın Kayıp Markiz Vakası adlı kitabı ustaca kurgulanmış bir roman. Sinemaya uyarlanmasında ise senarist Jack Thorne ve yönetmen Harry Bradbeer rol oynuyor. Özellikle erkek egemen toplumun gölgesinde kalmış kadınların geleceğe ışık tutabilecek adımlar atabildiklerini göstermek açısından çok önemli bir film olduğunu düşünüyorum.</p>



<p>Hepimiz hem edebiyat hem de sinemada Sherlock Holmes adını defalarca duyduk. Sherlock, kıvrak zekası ve araştırmacı yönüyle bir sürü davayı çözerken, şifrelerin içine gizlenmiş katilleri bulurken onu defalarca soluksuz okuduk ve izledik.</p>



<p>Sherlock'un bir kız kardeşi var: Enola Holmes. Annesinin kelime oyunlarına olan merakı adını ''Alone'' yani yalnız kelimesinin tersi olarak koymasını sağlamış. Fakat Elona ismi gerçekten bir kelime oyunu olarak mı koyuldu? Bu sorunun cevabını filmin sonunda öğreniyoruz. </p>



<p>Film Londra'da geçen bir dönem filmi. Hal böyle olunca klasik Holmes kitaplarında/filmlerinde karşımıza çıkan direkt bir davanın çözülmesi olayı yok. Bu defa dava çok daha büyük. Holmes ailesinin babaları öldükten sonra, Enola'nın abileri Mycroft ve Sherlock' da evden ayrılmışlar. Enola ve annesi yıllarca birlikte yaşamışlar. Oldukça eğlenceli, kurallardan ve kalıplardan uzak güzel bir hayatları olduğunu düşünüyorlar. Enola evde eğitim görüyor ve küçük yaştan beri birbirinden farklı türlerde kitaplar okuyarak;fizik, matematik, edebiyat, kimya ve dövüş, spor gibi alanlarda annesi tarafından eğitim alıyor. Fakat Enola'nın 16. yaş günü sabahı annesi ardında çiçek kartlarının ve çeşitli eşyaların bulunduğu bir sandık bırakarak ortadan kayboluyor. Olaylar buradan sonra başlıyor.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/WhatsApp-Image-2020-09-23-at-14.08.43.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-4045" width="617" height="449"/></figure>



<p>Enola, abileri Mycrof ve Sherlock'a gelmeleri için haber veriyor. Sherlock, ailesine yeteri kadar önem göstermeden tek başına bir hayat sürerken Mycroft ise annesi ve kız kardeşine destek sağlıyor aynı zamanda da Enola'nın vasisi. Mycroft, Enola'nın giyinişini, hareketlerini, eğitimini beğenmediği bu durumda koca bulamayacağını söyleyerek onu yatılı bir zarafet okuluna yazdırıyor. Enola, annesinin ona söylediği sözlerden ve bıraktığı çiçek kartlarından çıkan ''ENOLA KASIMPATILARIMA İYİ BAK'' yazılı bir kağıt buluyor. Bu kağıt onu annesinin sakladığı ipuçlarına götürüyor ve Enola o gece evden kaçarak Londra'ya annesini bulmaya gidiyor.</p>



<p> Kılık değiştirerek bindiği trende Basilwether Markisi Lord Tewksbury ile karşılaşıyor. Lord ailesinden kaçıyor çünkü onların verdiği görevlerin ona ağır geldiğini, olmak istediği kişiden emin olmadığını söylüyor fakat peşinden bir adam onu öldürmek için trene biniyor. Yolda katili atlatıp trenden atlayarak uzun bir yolculuk sonunda Londra'ya varıyorlar. Enola, Tewksbury'nin aslında aptal olmadığını fark ediyor fakat Londra' da yollarını ayırıyorlar. Enola kılık değiştirip bir pansiyona yerleşiyor. Annesinin her gün okuduğu gazetelere gizli kelimelerle mesaj bırakıyor. Aklında kalan ipuçlarıyla onu takip ediyor ve her nasılsa lordun peşindeki katil onu buluyor. Bu olaylardan sonra Enola, lordu bulmaya ve yardım etmeye karar veriyor. Önce malikaneye bir dul şeklinde gidiyor. İlk olarak şüphelendiği kişi, lordun amcası oluyor. Bu sırada Enola'nın abileri de onu arıyorlar ayrıca Sherlock başta kabul etmediği Markiz davasının Enola tarafından ilgilenildiğini öğrenince o da bu davaya bakmaya başlıyor. Londra'da çalkantılı günler var. Gazeteler sürekli reformdan bahsediyor. Herkes için oy hakkı!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/WhatsApp-Image-2020-09-23-at-14.08.43-1-1024x429.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-4046"/></figure>



<p> Annesinin amacını tam olarak çözemeyen Enola, sonunda Mycroft tarafından bulunarak zarafet okuluna gönderiliyor. Fakat burada çok kalmıyor Lord Tewksbury gelip onu gizli bir şekilde oradan çıkartıyor. Okuldan kaçarken karşılarına iki yol çıkıyor; ya cesaret isteyeni yapacak ve düzeni değiştirecek ya da sadece kendini kurtaracak. Enola doğru olanı yaparak, Basilwether' e gidiyor. Burada lordun peşindeki katille bir mücadeleye girişiyorlar.  Ve katil olarada ölüyor. Tam o sırada lordun büyükannesi gelerek onlara ateş ediyor. Tabi ikisine de bir şey olmuyor ve büyükanne tutuklanıyor. Sherlock davayı Enola'dan sonra çözüyor ve kardeşinin ne kadar zeki ve başarılı olduğunu keşfediyor. Onun vasisliğini üstleniyor. </p>



<p>Bu arada filmin başından sonuna kadar geçen reform oylaması günü geliyor. Lord' da katılımcılar arasında. Lord'un oyu belirleyici oluyor ve Enola sayesinde reform ve kadınlar için oy hakkı geliyor.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote has-text-align-center"><p>Holmes olmak için yolunu bulmalısın</p></blockquote>



<p>Enola'nın kendini bulma yolculuğunu izledik. Kendini bulurken, dünyayı değiştirdi. Abilerinin gölgesinde, Holmes adı yüzünden ünlü olarak değil, Enola olarak bir şeyleri değiştirdi. Geleceğini kendi seçimleri ve mücadelesi, özgürlük savaşı belirledi. Kadınların sadece evlenmek ve çocuk doğurmak için var olmadıklarını dünyayı değiştirmek için adım atabileceklerini gösterdi.  Çünkü erkek egemen toplumun bizlere yansıttığı biz kadınlardan beklediği şey bu. Fakat Enola bunu değiştirdi. </p>



<p>Dönemsel olarak kıyafetleri ve mekanları uygun bulsam da ön plana çıkan gazete baskılarında hatalar olduğunu düşünüyorum. Çünkü o dönemin gazetelerine bakıldığı zaman gözle görülür farklılıklar görmek mümkün.</p>



<p>Enola'nın da dediği gibi GELECEK ELİMİZDE! </p>



<p>Not: Film hakkında görüşlerinizi bizimle paylaşmayı unutmayın</p>$tag4$ WHERE slug = 'enola-holmes-film-analizi';
UPDATE posts SET content = $tag4$<p class="has-text-align-center">When you read Odysseia, known as one of Homer's great works, you will see countless characters. In this work, which tells about the adventures of Odysseus and his friends returning from the Trojan War, you may be interested in a character who remained in the shadow of a man: the witch-goddess Kirke, who hosted Odysseus and his friends on his holy island - or imprisoned - for a year.</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center">Especially after the book Ben Kirke written by Madeline Miller, this goddess, a character that faded into the dusty pages of history, attracted the attention of recent readers. Although it is difficult to observe the woman who was positioned as witch, dark and evil in front of the man in past myths and narrate the events by constructing them from her mouth, it also gives us the chance to evaluate the events from a different perspective. In this respect, the book's ability to look at us from a different shore and its more moderate approach to women in both mythology and mythology offered a different option for new readers and mythology enthusiasts.</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center">Let's come to this story of the noble witch Helios, who was rescued from the dusty shelves and shining again … When her family is examined, Helios, who is a Titan, and Okeanos, who is also another Titan, appear as one of four children from the sea nympha Perseis. These four brothers, the son of a father who lost his old power after the great war and a mother who could not break away from water, have a different power as of their time: They know the language of plants. This herbal science, which has been described with various names such as husband-wife medicine, poison, and magic, and which caused women to be burned and stigmatized as unbelievers even thousands of years after these narratives, is a rebellion against the divine power and might of its time. Because the gods do not need to resort to them to get what they want, but these noble brothers of Helios possess a knowledge that even the gods do not know. This causes them to be labeled dangerous. In addition, these beings that look like human beings and speak like human beings even though they come from titans cause people to be afraid of them. As explained in the Odyssey:</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center">"We left and finally reached Aiaie Island,</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>Kirke used to sit there, pretty certain,</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>scary goddess with human voice</em>"</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery aligncenter has-nested-images columns-default">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/circe-magic.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3863"/></figure>
</figure>



<p class="has-text-align-center">With this definition, it is necessary to know that the other three brothers of Kirke are not very good beings in the Greek world: One of them is the sorceress Aietes, the king of Colchis, whom Lason kidnapped his golden coat and killed his son; his wife is Pasiphae, the other is Perses, who caused family disaster for power. Having a family tree full of such negative examples, Kirke is also known for turning the men who came to his island into animals, which he did to the soldiers who came with Odysseus. However, there is a situation that is ignored here, or rather, is not mentioned in order to highlight the witch woman, which is the greed of these men. To punish these greedy men, Kirke turns them into pigs - there is also a good Ghibli movie to reference: Spirited Away.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery aligncenter has-nested-images columns-default">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/circewitch1-1024x795-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3864"/></figure>
</figure>



<p class="has-text-align-center">Of course, Kirke falls in love with Odysseus, who is depicted as cunning and handsome, as would be expected in a male literature, and tells him that he will turn his friends into old disguise in exchange for staying with him. Odysseus promises and keeps his word for a year. During this time, although she lives like a king on the island of the woman, she cannot bear the pressure of her surroundings and the longing of her wife and son who are waiting for her at home and decides to leave the island. It is also possible to see how much Kirke helped Odysseus here. He tells him how his return home will take place and does his best to help with the journey. According to the ongoing narratives, the children he made from the outgoing Odysseus became Telegonos, who founded the city of Tusculum, and Latinos, who was accepted as the father of the Latins. Even though Kirke takes place as a witch in all narratives, she is actually a woman who does not spare the help of those who come to her. He even helped his nephew Medea.</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center">When the character of Kirke is examined, her connection with both wild animals and soil and plants may cause her to be positioned like a land goddess. It has a connection with Kybele or Artemis, the goddess of Anatolia, in terms of character and features. In addition, considering the period when Odyssey was written, the Gilgamesh Epic, which has reached many people, has an effect on the myth of Kirke. Kirke is the intertwining of Siduri in Gilgamesh and Ishtar. This makes her duality clear: she is both a healer woman who helps everyone, and a witch who spells, is dark and harms men.</p>



<p class="has-text-align-center">In other words, Kirke, which Homer conveyed to us, is that goddess who was declared bad for coming from the heart of Anatolia and the Middle East. In the face of the noble and unique powerful power of men, it is the existence of the woman who takes her source from the soil and tradition. And no matter how he tried to disparage him, he won this conflict with his own compassion and good will.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery aligncenter has-nested-images columns-default">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/a2be1d223b1299bfc5e8a8abe5c77515-1-625x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3866"/></figure>
</figure>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>"I know, you suffered so much in the sea with fish,</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>you saw so much evil from enemy men on land,</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>but come and eat those food, drink those wines</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>let your heart come alive all over again,</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>be bold like when you first broke up,</em></p>



<p class="has-text-align-center"><em>from that fatherland, that rocky Ithake!</em></p>



<p><strong>SOURCE</strong></p>



<p><em>Odysseia- Homeros</em></p>



<p><em>Ben, Kirke- Madeline Miller</em></p>



<p><em>Hey Koca Yurt- Halikarnas Balıkçısı</em></p>



<p><em>Mitoloji Sözlüğü- Azra Erhat</em></p>$tag4$ WHERE slug = 'reshaped-goddess-kirke';
UPDATE posts SET content = $tag4$<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;During the quarantine days we all give ourselves to watching something - TV shows, competitions, movies - we sometimes find ourselves in what we're watching. Maybe even your family members are having that moment. And our affair starts here: in a place where we call 'It's like living that moment'.</p>



<p>We always look for the reason to be caught up in it. Frankly, we do not pay much attention because crying for a character who died in a movie, getting excited as if he was really competing in a competition, being loving in a romantic scene of the series are actually feelings we all experience. Now let's get to the bottom of these emotions we experience, namely mirror neurons to enable us to experience them.</p>



<p>Something was discovered by chance in an experiment to study the movements in monkeys' brains. When a monkey doing nothing watched a monkey eating a banana, they noticed that the same neurons were active in both monkeys. In other words, the ape that did nothing seem to be eating a banana, and there was movement in the neurons in his brain. However, he was just watching the actual monkey eating a banana. Scientists wanted to be sure of the existence of mirror neurons to prove their accuracy with other tests. They found that there was the same brain activation in many motor functions, not just when eating a banana. This was a very interesting discovery for them, because literally, apes had mimetic neurons in their brains that were activated without acting. Well, if there were apes that were most likened to humans, did we have the same thing?</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/ayna-noronlar-1024x555-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3811" width="639" height="345"/></figure>



<p>They tried it on epilepsy patients because they were reluctant to do the experiment on healthy people and found it difficult. And the result was just like the apes, so when we see someone eating a banana or using any motor function, the same neurons are activated as that person.</p>



<p>&nbsp;&nbsp; When you look at it now, it may be easier to make sense of things actually. For example, we have known for years that yawning is contagious or that we are affected by movies, series and competitions that we have just mentioned, sometimes even if you are not hungry, your appetite suddenly rises while you are eating, and when a negative person enters your friend environment, you also exploit your energy … Actually, all of them are because we have mirror neurons. . We owe all and more of these events to their ability to imitate. Even the thought that even languages may have developed thanks to 'mimetic' neurons is not in the middle.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Makak_neonatal_imitation-1-1024x392.png" alt="" class="wp-image-3812" width="743" height="284"/></figure>



<p>&nbsp;So who benefits best from these neurons? In my opinion, parents who have children, of course. Because when the child is born, he is kind of unaware of everything. It learns everything from you and the environment over time by living, seeing, examining and observing. Love, happiness, sadness, pain… Actually, as a parent, you are still shaping your child - apart from genetics, of course.</p>



<p> For example, if you smoke and your child sees this constantly, you cannot expect him to stop smoking in the future. Because there is a scientific fact called mirror neurons! Already, when you drink, your child's already activated by imitating the same neurons. Besides, it would not be right to expect this from an ethical point of view, apart from the scientific truth.</p>



<div class="wp-block-jetpack-tiled-gallery aligncenter is-style-rectangular"><div class="tiled-gallery__gallery"><div class="tiled-gallery__row"><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:52.74601482086286%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="" data-height="617" data-id="3817" data-link="https://www.loveinartsz.com/?attachment_id=3817" data-url="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/brain.jpg" data-width="1000" src="https://i2.wp.com/www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/brain.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div><div class="tiled-gallery__col" style="flex-basis:47.25398517913713%"><figure class="tiled-gallery__item"><img alt="" data-height="689" data-id="3814" data-link="https://www.loveinartsz.com/?attachment_id=3814" data-url="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/5d78d6d64d1ba-1.jpg" data-width="1000" src="https://i1.wp.com/www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/5d78d6d64d1ba-1.jpg?ssl=1" data-amp-layout="responsive"/></figure></div></div></div></div>



<p>Or let's look at reading books, the most obsessive subject of parents. If you are a parent who has never opened the cover of the book, it is not right to constantly print 'read' to your child. Because it's still the same. Your child and its mirror neurons will take you as an example until a certain age - until they open up to the environment. For a while, you are both friends, family and everything. So he tends to do whatever he sees from you, idolizes you, you are a powerful source of authority for him. Apart from these, the mirror neurons that we talk about all the time are active and alert to imitate you.</p>



<p>In other words, our mirror neurons, which no one predicts that the effect will be so great as you will understand, actually has a really important place in every aspect of our lives. Even I can give you an example of mirror neurons from my own memories:</p>



<p>I was a student who had nothing to do with the kitchen until I went to college and even had a home in college. Pasta, eggs etc. I hadn't touched anything other than simple things like But I remember watching my mom do something in the kitchen since I was little. Usually when he was doing something, we would talk about what happened during the day or other topics - of course, I would tell and observe him most of the time. Of course, my observation periods would vary depending on the events that happened that day or our desire to talk, sometimes short, sometimes long, and sometimes little help. After I got home at college - that moment when you realized you were going to be hungry - I called my mother and asked for a recipe that could be made with home ingredients. Of course, my pace of doing it normally was slow because I had no experience. But I noticed that I still had a strange dexterity. And seriously, even though it was the first meal I made - not exactly like my mom's - it was very close to her meal. As if my mother was describing how to cook the food, she was visualizing her chopping things up, the spices she dreamed of… In this case, I realized later that mirror neurons were also effective. Because while I was watching my mother cooking, the same neurons were activated in me as if I was doing it. However, I was watching my mother do. So here I was like a child encouraged by his mother to read. Of course, the mother in my analogy was someone who read a book, not just encouraging with words. I was also a child affected by my observations and longed to read a book after a while.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img src="https://www.loveinartsz.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/ayna-noronlar-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3816" width="402" height="311"/></figure>



<p>I usually gave examples from children, but if we assume that I am 20 years old in my own example, we actually learn something in life. Even if I say children are the most advantageous, people who are still hungry to learn have an advantage as well. We just need to be aware of our neurons!</p>



<p>Remember, you have neurons in your brain that mimic everyone else, and they can be influenced by your environment. Now it's up to you to learn the existence of these neurons and use them. Let's see if you are still hungry to learn something new.</p>



<p>Yararlanılan ve İnceleyebileceğiniz Kaynaklar:</p>



